# ── `k2 agent hire` built-in persona archetypes (S3) ─────────────────
#
# Embedded in the CLI on purpose: hire is a CLI-side COMPOSITION of
# existing daemon routes (PRD §3), and the daemon's /cli/agents/create
# default scaffold remains the no-flag fallback — these four skeletons
# are hire-only sugar, so the CLI is their simplest maintainable home.
# Each is a short charter: role + reporting line, a K2 comms block,
# explicit do-NOTs, and an escalation-contact placeholder the operator
# fills in on day one. The persona machinery (backups etc.) treats them
# exactly like a user-supplied --persona file.
_agent_template_body() {
    case "$1" in
        worker) cat <<'EOF'
## Role

You are a WORKER agent: you execute well-scoped tasks end-to-end and
report the outcome. You report to: __MANAGER__ (replace with your
manager agent's name).

## How you work

- Take ONE task at a time; finish it before picking up the next.
- Verify your own work before reporting done — run it, test it, read
  it back. "It should work" is not done.
- Keep a short running work log in your workspace so a re-launched
  session can pick up your context.
- If you are blocked for more than ~15 minutes, say so — don't spin.

## Communications (K2 CLI)

- `k2 inbox` — check your inbox at the start of every session.
- `k2 talk <agent> "message"` — interactive send: shows the peer's
  live screen first, then delivers. Use when you need a reply.
- `k2 msg <agent> "message"` — direct delivery to a live peer.
- `k2 msg <agent> --inbox --title "..." --body "..."` — queued inbox
  item for a peer that may be asleep.
- `k2 feedback ask "<title>"` — ask your HUMAN for a decision or an
  approval; the ask sits durably on their Feedback page (it does not
  die like a terminal prompt) and the answer comes back to you.
- `k2 project read` / `k2 project msg <name> "..."` — your project's
  shared group chat. A message prefixed `[project:<name>]` came from
  there: reply with `k2 project msg <name> "..."`, NEVER `k2 msg
  <name>` (a Project is a group of workspaces, not a workspace —
  `k2 msg` fails with workspace_not_found).
- `k2 checkin` — your workspace's status + pending-work summary.

## Do NOT

- Do NOT take on work outside the task's scope without asking first.
- Do NOT answer another agent's human-in-the-loop prompt — back off
  and let its owner handle it.
- Do NOT push to shared branches, rotate credentials, or touch
  infrastructure unless the task explicitly says so.
- Do NOT go silent when blocked or uncertain.

## Escalation

When blocked, uncertain, or the task itself looks wrong: STOP and
message your escalation contact: __ESCALATION_CONTACT__ (replace with
a real agent name or your owner on day one).
EOF
            ;;
        manager) cat <<'EOF'
## Role

You are a MANAGER agent: you break goals into tasks, delegate them to
connected worker agents, track progress, and report upward. You report
to: __ESCALATION_CONTACT__ (your operator/owner — replace this).

## How you work

- Keep a live task board (a simple markdown file in this workspace):
  who owns what, current status, next checkpoint.
- Delegate OUTCOMES, not keystrokes — let workers own their approach;
  hold them to the result.
- Follow up on anything you delegated that has gone quiet.
- Summarize status upward on request in under 10 lines.

## Communications (K2 CLI)

- `k2 connections list` — the agents you can reach from here.
- `k2 agent list` — the full roster on this server.
- `k2 talk <agent> "message"` — interactive send: read the peer's
  live screen, then deliver. Use for delegation and follow-ups.
- `k2 msg <agent> --inbox --title "..." --body "..."` — queued task
  for an agent that may be asleep.
- `k2 feedback ask "<title>"` — ask your HUMAN for a decision or an
  approval; the ask sits durably on their Feedback page (it does not
  die like a terminal prompt) and the answer comes back to you.
- `k2 project read` / `k2 project msg <name> "..."` — your project's
  shared group chat. A message prefixed `[project:<name>]` came from
  there: reply with `k2 project msg <name> "..."`, NEVER `k2 msg
  <name>` (a Project is a group of workspaces, not a workspace —
  `k2 msg` fails with workspace_not_found).
- `k2 inbox` — check your own inbox at the start of every session.

## Do NOT

- Do NOT do the workers' tasks yourself — if you keep doing a job,
  flag that the team needs a hire instead.
- Do NOT reconfigure or retire agents (`k2 agent set` / `k2 agent
  retire`) without your owner's instruction.
- Do NOT answer a worker's human-in-the-loop prompt you don't have
  standing over.
- Do NOT let a task sit unassigned without telling your owner.

## Escalation

Anything outside your delegation authority — hiring, retiring,
spending, credentials, production changes — goes to:
__ESCALATION_CONTACT__ (replace on day one).
EOF
            ;;
        qa) cat <<'EOF'
## Role

You are a QA agent: you verify other agents' work against its stated
intent and report findings. You report to: __MANAGER__ (replace with
your manager agent's name).

## How you work

- Start from what the change CLAIMS to do; test the claim first, then
  the edges around it.
- Reproduce before you report — every finding comes with exact steps.
- Rate every finding: blocker / bug / nit. Never inflate severity.
- "Passed" means YOU ran it and watched it work — never mark passed
  on faith.

## Communications (K2 CLI)

- `k2 inbox` — incoming review requests land here; check every session.
- `k2 talk <agent> "message"` — send findings to the owning agent and
  discuss interactively.
- `k2 msg <agent> --inbox --title "..." --body "..."` — queued
  findings report for an agent that may be asleep.
- `k2 feedback ask "<title>"` — ask your HUMAN for a decision or an
  approval; the ask sits durably on their Feedback page (it does not
  die like a terminal prompt) and the answer comes back to you.
- `k2 project read` / `k2 project msg <name> "..."` — your project's
  shared group chat. A message prefixed `[project:<name>]` came from
  there: reply with `k2 project msg <name> "..."`, NEVER `k2 msg
  <name>` (a Project is a group of workspaces, not a workspace —
  `k2 msg` fails with workspace_not_found).
- `k2 checkin` — your workspace's status + pending-work summary.

## Do NOT

- Do NOT fix the code yourself — report to the owning agent; you
  verify, they fix.
- Do NOT approve work you only read but did not run.
- Do NOT answer another agent's human-in-the-loop prompt.
- Do NOT soften findings to be agreeable — precise and neutral beats
  polite and vague.

## Escalation

Blockers the owning agent disputes, or anything that looks like data
loss / security exposure: escalate immediately to
__ESCALATION_CONTACT__ (replace on day one).
EOF
            ;;
        researcher) cat <<'EOF'
## Role

You are a RESEARCHER agent: you investigate questions, compare
options, and produce short, sourced write-ups. You report to:
__MANAGER__ (replace with your manager agent's name).

## How you work

- Restate the question AND the decision it feeds before digging.
- Prefer primary sources; note the retrieval date on anything volatile
  (pricing, versions, benchmarks).
- Deliverable shape: a 5–15 line summary up top, details + sources
  below.
- Say "unknown" when the evidence is thin — a marked gap is worth
  more than a confident guess.

## Communications (K2 CLI)

- `k2 inbox` — research requests land here; check every session.
- `k2 talk <agent> "message"` — deliver findings and discuss
  interactively.
- `k2 msg <agent> --inbox --title "..." --body "..."` — queued
  write-up for an agent that may be asleep.
- `k2 feedback ask "<title>"` — ask your HUMAN for a decision or an
  approval; the ask sits durably on their Feedback page (it does not
  die like a terminal prompt) and the answer comes back to you.
- `k2 project read` / `k2 project msg <name> "..."` — your project's
  shared group chat. A message prefixed `[project:<name>]` came from
  there: reply with `k2 project msg <name> "..."`, NEVER `k2 msg
  <name>` (a Project is a group of workspaces, not a workspace —
  `k2 msg` fails with workspace_not_found).
- `k2 checkin` — your workspace's status + pending-work summary.

## Do NOT

- Do NOT modify code, configs, or infrastructure — you produce
  knowledge, not changes.
- Do NOT present speculation as fact; label confidence explicitly.
- Do NOT pad reports — if it fits in 10 lines, deliver 10 lines.
- Do NOT answer another agent's human-in-the-loop prompt.

## Escalation

Questions you cannot source, or requests that would need real
spending/credentials to answer: escalate to __ESCALATION_CONTACT__
(replace on day one).
EOF
            ;;
        *) return 1 ;;
    esac
}

# `k2 agent hire <dir>` — S3. One atomic, idempotent call composing the
# EXISTING routes (PRD §3): mkdir → persona (template | file | the
# /cli/agents/create default scaffold) → /cli/workspace/open →
# /cli/workspace/set (mode/enabled) → set-agent-display-name (--name;
# writes BOTH name stores) → /cli/connections per edge →
# ensure-canonical-session (--launch) → /cli/workspace/msg (--onboard).
# Re-running converges: satisfied steps report skipped(reason) and the
# whole call reports changed:false — which is also the crash-recovery
# story (a failed run is re-run to finish).
cmd_agent_hire() {
    if _wants_help "$@"; then cmd_help_agent_hire; exit 0; fi
    local dir="" name="" template="" persona="" mode="" enabled="" onboard=""
    local launch=false dry_run=false as_json=false
    local connects=()
    while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
        case "$1" in
            --name)
                [ $# -ge 2 ] || { _agent_err "bad_usage" "--name requires a value"; exit 2; }
                name="$2"; shift 2 ;;
            --template)
                [ $# -ge 2 ] || { _agent_err "bad_usage" "--template requires a value (worker | manager | qa | researcher)"; exit 2; }
                template="$2"; shift 2 ;;
            --persona)
                [ $# -ge 2 ] || { _agent_err "bad_usage" "--persona requires a file path"; exit 2; }
                persona="$2"; shift 2 ;;
            --mode)
                [ $# -ge 2 ] || { _agent_err "bad_usage" "--mode requires a value (off | custom | manager | k2)"; exit 2; }
                mode="$2"; shift 2 ;;
            --enabled)
                [ $# -ge 2 ] || { _agent_err "bad_usage" "--enabled requires a value (true | false)"; exit 2; }
                enabled="$2"; shift 2 ;;
            --connect)
                [ $# -ge 2 ] || { _agent_err "bad_usage" "--connect requires an agent name"; exit 2; }
                connects+=("$2"); shift 2 ;;
            --launch) launch=true; shift ;;
            --onboard)
                [ $# -ge 2 ] || { _agent_err "bad_usage" "--onboard requires a message"; exit 2; }
                onboard="$2"; shift 2 ;;
            --dry-run) dry_run=true; shift ;;
            --json) as_json=true; shift ;;
            -*)
                _agent_err "bad_usage" "unknown flag '$1' — see: k2 agent hire --help"
                exit 2 ;;
            *)
                if [ -z "$dir" ]; then dir="$1"; else
                    _agent_err "bad_usage" "unexpected extra argument '$1' — usage: k2 agent hire <dir> [flags]"
                    exit 2
                fi
                shift ;;
        esac
    done
    if [ -z "$dir" ]; then
        _agent_err "bad_usage" "missing <dir> — usage: k2 agent hire <dir> [flags] (see: k2 agent hire --help)"
        exit 2
    fi
    if [ -n "$template" ] && [ -n "$persona" ]; then
        _agent_err "bad_usage" "--template and --persona are mutually exclusive — pass one or the other"
        exit 2
    fi
    local template_body=""
    if [ -n "$template" ]; then
        template_body=$(_agent_template_body "$template") || {
            _agent_err "bad_usage" "unknown template '$template' — valid: worker, manager, qa, researcher"
            exit 2
        }
    fi
    if [ -n "$persona" ] && { [ ! -f "$persona" ] || [ ! -r "$persona" ]; }; then
        _agent_err "bad_usage" "persona file not found or unreadable: $persona"
        exit 2
    fi
    case "$mode" in
        ""|off|custom|manager|k2|k2so) ;;
        *)
            _agent_err "bad_usage" "invalid --mode '$mode' — valid: off, custom, manager, k2"
            exit 2 ;;
    esac
    case "$enabled" in
        ""|true|false) ;;
        *)
            _agent_err "bad_usage" "invalid --enabled '$enabled' — valid: true, false"
            exit 2 ;;
    esac
    # --onboard implies --launch (mockup contract).
    [ -n "$onboard" ] && launch=true

    local connects_json
    connects_json=$(python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.dumps(sys.argv[1:]))' \
        ${connects[@]+"${connects[@]}"})

    HIRE_DIR="$dir" NAME="$name" TEMPLATE="$template" TEMPLATE_BODY="$template_body" \
    PERSONA_FILE="$persona" MODE="$mode" ENABLED="$enabled" CONNECTS="$connects_json" \
    LAUNCH="$launch" ONBOARD="$onboard" DRY_RUN="$dry_run" \
    AS_JSON="$as_json" ABASE="$BASE_URL" ATOKEN="$TOKEN" python3 - <<'PYEOF'
import json, os, re, sys
import urllib.error, urllib.parse, urllib.request

dir_arg = os.environ["HIRE_DIR"]
name = os.environ.get("NAME", "")
template = os.environ.get("TEMPLATE", "")
template_body = os.environ.get("TEMPLATE_BODY", "")
persona_file = os.environ.get("PERSONA_FILE", "")
mode = os.environ.get("MODE", "")
enabled = os.environ.get("ENABLED", "")
connects = json.loads(os.environ.get("CONNECTS", "[]"))
launch = os.environ.get("LAUNCH") == "true"
onboard = os.environ.get("ONBOARD", "")
dry_run = os.environ.get("DRY_RUN") == "true"
as_json = os.environ.get("AS_JSON") == "true"
base = os.environ["ABASE"]
token = os.environ["ATOKEN"]

path = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(dir_arg))

def fail(code, hint, exit_code=1):
    sys.stderr.write(json.dumps({"error": {"code": code, "hint": hint}}) + "\n")
    sys.exit(exit_code)

if os.path.exists(path) and not os.path.isdir(path):
    fail("bad_usage", "%s exists and is not a directory" % path, 2)

def http_get(route, params, timeout=30):
    qs = urllib.parse.urlencode(dict(params, token=token))
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(base + route + "?" + qs, timeout=timeout) as r:
            return json.loads(r.read().decode("utf-8", "replace"))
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        try:
            return json.loads(e.read().decode("utf-8", "replace"))
        except Exception:
            return {"error": "HTTP %s on %s" % (e.code, route)}
    except Exception as e:
        return {"error": "%s: %s" % (route, e)}

def http_post_json(route, body, timeout=30):
    url = base + route + "?token=" + urllib.parse.quote(token, safe="")
    req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=json.dumps(body).encode(),
                                 headers={"Content-Type": "application/json"}, method="POST")
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as r:
            return json.loads(r.read().decode("utf-8", "replace"))
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        try:
            return json.loads(e.read().decode("utf-8", "replace"))
        except Exception:
            return {"error": "HTTP %s on %s" % (e.code, route)}
    except Exception as e:
        return {"error": "%s: %s" % (route, e)}

# ── Probe current state (this is what makes hire idempotent) ─────
conf = http_get("/cli/agent/conf", {"q": path})
probe_err = conf.get("error")
if probe_err:
    if isinstance(probe_err, dict) and probe_err.get("code") == "not_found":
        pass  # unregistered — hire is about to register it
    else:
        hint = probe_err.get("hint") if isinstance(probe_err, dict) else str(probe_err)
        fail("daemon_error", "cannot probe %s: %s" % (path, hint))
registered = bool(conf.get("ok"))

dir_exists = os.path.isdir(path)
basename = os.path.basename(path.rstrip("/")) or "agent"
# The technical agent name (frontmatter name:, /cli/agents/create) —
# same sanitization the S2 persona scaffold uses.
agent_name = re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9_-]", "-", basename) or "agent"

persona_path = conf.get("personaPath") if registered else None
if not persona_path:
    for dot in (".k2", ".k2so"):
        cand = os.path.join(path, dot, "agent", "AGENT.md")
        if os.path.isfile(cand):
            persona_path = cand
            break
persona_exists = bool(persona_path)

persona_content = None
if persona_file:
    try:
        with open(persona_file, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
            persona_content = f.read()
    except OSError as e:
        fail("bad_usage", "cannot read persona file %s: %s" % (persona_file, e), 2)
elif template:
    # Full AGENT.md: generated frontmatter + the archetype charter body.
    fm = "name: %s\nrole: %s\ntype: %s" % (
        agent_name, template, "manager" if template == "manager" else "agent-template")
    if template == "manager":
        fm += "\nmanager: true"
    persona_content = "---\n%s\n---\n\n# Persona — %s\n\n%s\n" % (
        fm, name or basename, template_body.strip())

desired_mode = mode or "custom"
# CLI-canonical spelling (k2so accepted as a back-compat alias).
desired_mode = {"k2so": "k2"}.get(desired_mode, desired_mode)

existing_peers = set()
live = False
if registered:
    for c in conf.get("connections") or []:
        p = c.get("peer")
        if p:
            existing_peers.add(p.lower())
    live = bool((conf.get("live") or {}).get("active"))

# ── Build the plan ───────────────────────────────────────────────
actions = []
if dir_exists:
    actions.append({"step": "create-dir", "status": "skipped", "reason": "exists"})
else:
    actions.append({"step": "create-dir", "status": "pending"})

wp = {"step": "write-persona"}
if template:
    wp["template"] = template
elif persona_file:
    wp["source"] = persona_file
else:
    wp["source"] = "default-scaffold"
if persona_exists:
    # Hire heals MISSING pieces; replacing an existing persona is
    # `k2 agent set --persona`'s job (with backups).
    wp.update(status="skipped", reason="exists")
else:
    wp["status"] = "pending"
actions.append(wp)

actions.append(
    {"step": "register-workspace", "status": "skipped", "reason": "already-registered"}
    if registered else {"step": "register-workspace", "status": "pending"})

if registered and conf.get("mode") == desired_mode:
    actions.append({"step": "set-mode", "mode": desired_mode,
                    "status": "skipped", "reason": "already %s" % desired_mode})
else:
    actions.append({"step": "set-mode", "mode": desired_mode, "status": "pending"})

if enabled:
    want = enabled == "true"
    if registered and bool(conf.get("enabled")) == want and (desired_mode == conf.get("mode")):
        actions.append({"step": "set-enabled", "enabled": want,
                        "status": "skipped", "reason": "already %s" % enabled})
    else:
        actions.append({"step": "set-enabled", "enabled": want, "status": "pending"})

if name:
    if registered and conf.get("name") == name:
        actions.append({"step": "set-name", "name": name,
                        "status": "skipped", "reason": "already named %s" % name})
    else:
        actions.append({"step": "set-name", "name": name, "status": "pending"})

for peer in connects:
    # Connections are always mutual: the substrate stores ONE row per
    # pair (migration 0051 — a single row IS bidirectional awareness).
    if peer.lower() in existing_peers:
        actions.append({"step": "connect", "peer": peer, "status": "skipped",
                        "reason": "edge exists", "bidirectional": True})
    else:
        actions.append({"step": "connect", "peer": peer, "status": "pending",
                        "bidirectional": True})

if launch:
    if live:
        actions.append({"step": "launch", "status": "skipped", "reason": "already live"})
    else:
        actions.append({"step": "launch", "status": "pending"})

if onboard:
    # A message is imperative, not converging state: it sends on every
    # run that asks for it.
    actions.append({"step": "onboard", "status": "pending"})

display_name = name or (conf.get("name") if registered else basename) or basename

def emit(ok, changed):
    out = {"ok": ok, "changed": changed, "name": display_name, "path": path,
           "actions": actions}
    if dry_run:
        out["dryRun"] = True
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(out))
        return
    if dry_run:
        print("DRY RUN — no changes made. Plan for %s (%s):" % (display_name, path))
    for a in actions:
        step, status = a["step"], a["status"]
        if step == "create-dir":
            line = "create-dir: %s" % path
        elif step == "write-persona":
            if "template" in a:
                line = "write-persona: template '%s'" % a["template"]
            elif a.get("source") == "default-scaffold":
                line = "write-persona: default scaffold"
            else:
                line = "write-persona: from %s" % a.get("source")
        elif step == "register-workspace":
            line = "register-workspace"
        elif step == "set-mode":
            line = "mode: %s" % a["mode"]
        elif step == "set-enabled":
            line = "enabled: %s" % ("true" if a["enabled"] else "false")
        elif step == "set-name":
            line = "name: %s" % a["name"]
        elif step == "connect":
            line = "connect: %s (bidirectional)" % a["peer"]
        elif step == "launch":
            line = "launch"
            if a.get("sessionId"):
                line += " (session %s)" % str(a["sessionId"])[:8]
        else:
            line = "onboard: deliver first message"
        if status == "skipped" and a.get("reason"):
            line += "  (%s)" % a["reason"]
        marker = {"pending": "would apply", "done": "done", "skipped": "skipped",
                  "failed": "FAILED"}[status]
        print("  %-14s %s" % ("[" + marker + "]", line))
    if not dry_run:
        n = sum(1 for a in actions if a["status"] == "done")
        print("%s: %s" % (display_name,
                          ("%d change(s) applied." % n) if n else "no changes — already converged."))

if dry_run:
    emit(True, any(a["status"] == "pending" for a in actions))
    sys.exit(0)

changed = False

def step_failed(action, code, hint):
    action["status"] = "failed"
    emit(False, changed)
    fail(code, hint)

by_step = {}
for a in actions:
    by_step.setdefault(a["step"], []).append(a)

def one(step):
    lst = by_step.get(step) or [None]
    return lst[0]

# 1. create-dir
a = one("create-dir")
if a and a["status"] == "pending":
    try:
        os.makedirs(path, exist_ok=True)
    except OSError as e:
        step_failed(a, "fs_error", "cannot create %s: %s" % (path, e))
    a["status"] = "done"
    changed = True

# 2. write-persona
a = one("write-persona")
if a and a["status"] == "pending":
    # /cli/agents/create scaffolds the canonical .k2/agent/AGENT.md
    # (no-op when it exists); a template/--persona then writes through
    # /cli/agents/save-agent-md — the same backup-aware door
    # `k2 agent set --persona` uses.
    resp = http_get("/cli/agents/create",
                    {"project_path": path, "name": agent_name,
                     "role": template or ""})
    if isinstance(resp.get("error"), str) and resp["error"]:
        step_failed(a, "daemon_error", "persona scaffold failed: %s" % resp["error"])
    if persona_content is not None:
        resp = http_post_json("/cli/agents/save-agent-md",
                              {"project_path": path, "agent_name": agent_name,
                               "content": persona_content})
        if resp.get("error") or not resp.get("success"):
            step_failed(a, "daemon_error",
                        "persona write failed: %s" % resp.get("error", json.dumps(resp)[:300]))
    a["status"] = "done"
    changed = True

# 3. register-workspace
a = one("register-workspace")
if a and a["status"] == "pending":
    resp = http_get("/cli/workspace/open", {"path": path})
    err = resp.get("error")
    if isinstance(err, str) and "already registered" in err:
        a["status"] = "skipped"
        a["reason"] = "already-registered"
    elif err or not resp.get("success"):
        step_failed(a, "daemon_error",
                    "workspace registration failed: %s" % (err or json.dumps(resp)[:300]))
    else:
        a["status"] = "done"
        changed = True

# 4. set-mode + set-enabled in ONE /cli/workspace/set batch (the route
#    applies agent_mode first so an explicit enabled wins the coupling).
fields = {}
ma = one("set-mode")
if ma and ma["status"] == "pending":
    fields["agent_mode"] = ma["mode"]
ea = one("set-enabled")
if ea and ea["status"] == "pending":
    fields["agent_enabled"] = "1" if ea["enabled"] else "0"
if fields:
    resp = http_post_json("/cli/workspace/set", {"project": path, "fields": fields})
    if resp.get("error") or not resp.get("ok"):
        err = resp.get("error")
        hint = err if isinstance(err, str) else (err or {}).get("hint") or json.dumps(resp)[:300]
        bad = ma if (ma and ma["status"] == "pending") else ea
        step_failed(bad, "daemon_error", "settings write failed: %s" % hint)
    by_field = {x.get("field"): x.get("status") for x in resp.get("actions", [])}
    if ma and ma["status"] == "pending":
        ma["status"] = by_field.get("agent_mode", "done")
        if ma["status"] == "skipped":
            ma["reason"] = "already %s" % ma["mode"]
        changed = changed or ma["status"] == "done"
    if ea and ea["status"] == "pending":
        ea["status"] = by_field.get("agent_enabled", "done")
        if ea["status"] == "skipped":
            ea["reason"] = "already set"
        changed = changed or ea["status"] == "done"

# 5. set-name (writes BOTH name stores: AGENT.md display_name +
#    projects.name — addressing follows the rename).
a = one("set-name")
if a and a["status"] == "pending":
    resp = http_get("/cli/workspace/set-agent-display-name",
                    {"project_path": path, "name": a["name"]})
    if resp.get("error") or not resp.get("success"):
        step_failed(a, "daemon_error",
                    "rename failed: %s" % resp.get("error", json.dumps(resp)[:300]))
    a["status"] = "done"
    changed = True

# 6. connect edges. ONE add per peer: the connections substrate stores
#    a single row per pair and that row IS mutual awareness (migration
#    0051; the add-side reverse-pair guard no-ops redundant adds), so
#    there is no second direction to wire.
for a in by_step.get("connect", []):
    if a["status"] != "pending":
        continue
    peer = a["peer"]
    pconf = http_get("/cli/agent/conf", {"q": peer})
    if not pconf.get("ok"):
        err = pconf.get("error")
        hint = (err or {}).get("hint") if isinstance(err, dict) else err
        step_failed(a, "not_found" if isinstance(err, dict) and err.get("code") == "not_found"
                    else "daemon_error",
                    hint or "cannot resolve peer '%s'" % peer)
    peer_path = pconf["path"]
    if peer_path == path:
        step_failed(a, "bad_usage", "cannot connect %s to itself" % display_name)
    resp = http_get("/cli/connections",
                    {"action": "add", "project": path, "target": peer_path})
    if isinstance(resp.get("error"), str) and resp["error"]:
        step_failed(a, "daemon_error", "connect %s failed: %s" % (peer, resp["error"]))
    a["status"] = "done"
    changed = True

# 7. launch
a = one("launch")
if a and a["status"] == "pending":
    resp = http_get("/cli/workspace/ensure-canonical-session", {"project": path},
                    timeout=120)
    if resp.get("error") or not resp.get("success"):
        step_failed(a, "daemon_error",
                    "launch failed: %s" % resp.get("error", json.dumps(resp)[:300]))
    a["status"] = "done"
    a["sessionId"] = resp.get("session_id")
    if resp.get("reused"):
        a["reused"] = True
    else:
        changed = True

# 8. onboard (delivered via the same throat `k2 talk` uses —
#    /cli/workspace/msg with wake, which waits for READY first).
a = one("onboard")
if a and a["status"] == "pending":
    resp = http_get("/cli/workspace/msg",
                    {"workspace": path, "text": onboard, "from": "owner",
                     "wake": "true", "wake_timeout": "120"},
                    timeout=180)
    if isinstance(resp.get("error"), str) and resp["error"]:
        step_failed(a, "daemon_error", "onboard delivery failed: %s" % resp["error"])
    if not resp.get("success"):
        step_failed(a, "daemon_error",
                    "onboard delivery failed: %s" % (resp.get("message") or json.dumps(resp)[:300]))
    a["status"] = "done"
    changed = True

emit(True, changed)
PYEOF
}

# `k2 agent list` — S3. Reclaims the previously-deprecated arm with the
# real fleet-view semantics (PRD §3): every registered agent with mode,
# enabled, live-session status (same source as `conf`'s live), and path.
cmd_agent_list() {
    if _wants_help "$@"; then cmd_help_agent_list; exit 0; fi
    local as_json=false
    while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
        case "$1" in
            --json) as_json=true; shift ;;
            *)
                _agent_err "bad_usage" "unexpected argument '$1' — usage: k2 agent list [--json]"
                exit 2 ;;
        esac
    done
    local resp
    resp=$(cli_request "/cli/agent/list") || resp=""
    if [ -z "$resp" ]; then
        _agent_err "daemon_unreachable" "no response from the K2 daemon (is it running?)"
        exit 1
    fi
    RESP="$resp" AS_JSON="$as_json" python3 - <<'PYEOF'
import json, os, sys
raw = os.environ.get("RESP", "")
try:
    d = json.loads(raw)
except Exception:
    sys.stderr.write(json.dumps({"error": {"code": "bad_response",
        "hint": "daemon returned an unparseable response: %r" % raw[:200]}}) + "\n")
    sys.exit(1)
if d.get("error") or not d.get("ok"):
    err = d.get("error")
    if not isinstance(err, dict):
        err = {"code": "error", "hint": str(err or raw[:200])}
    sys.stderr.write(json.dumps({"error": err}) + "\n")
    sys.exit(1)
if os.environ.get("AS_JSON") == "true":
    print(json.dumps(d))
    sys.exit(0)

agents = d.get("agents") or []
if not agents:
    print("No agents registered on this server. Hire one: k2 agent hire <dir>")
    sys.exit(0)

home = os.path.expanduser("~")
def tilde(p):
    return "~" + p[len(home):] if p.startswith(home + "/") or p == home else p

rows = [("NAME", "MODE", "ENABLED", "LIVE", "PATH")]
for a in agents:
    rows.append((
        str(a.get("name", "?")),
        str(a.get("mode", "?")),
        "yes" if a.get("enabled") else "no",
        "yes" if a.get("live") else "no",
        tilde(str(a.get("path", "?"))),
    ))
widths = [max(len(r[i]) for r in rows) for i in range(4)]
for r in rows:
    print("%-*s  %-*s  %-*s  %-*s  %s" % (
        widths[0], r[0], widths[1], r[1], widths[2], r[2], widths[3], r[3], r[4]))
PYEOF
}

# `k2 agent retire <name>` — S4. Safe decommission via
# POST /cli/agent/retire: guards REFUSE (exit 3) on uncommitted/unpushed
# git work or likely secrets; --force overrides; --dry-run previews
# (mirroring the real verdict, including the exit code). On success the
# folder is ARCHIVED (never deleted), the registration + every
# connection edge + non-cascaded dependent rows are removed.
cmd_agent_retire() {
    if _wants_help "$@"; then cmd_help_agent_retire; exit 0; fi
    local name="" archive_to="" force=false dry_run=false as_json=false
    while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
        case "$1" in
            --archive-to)
                [ $# -ge 2 ] || { _agent_err "bad_usage" "--archive-to requires a directory"; exit 2; }
                archive_to="$2"; shift 2 ;;
            --force) force=true; shift ;;
            --dry-run) dry_run=true; shift ;;
            --json) as_json=true; shift ;;
            -*)
                _agent_err "bad_usage" "unknown flag '$1' — usage: k2 agent retire <name> [--archive-to <dir>] [--force] [--dry-run] [--json]"
                exit 2 ;;
            *)
                if [ -z "$name" ]; then name="$1"; else
                    _agent_err "bad_usage" "unexpected extra argument '$1' — usage: k2 agent retire <name> [flags]"
                    exit 2
                fi
                shift ;;
        esac
    done
    if [ -z "$name" ]; then
        _agent_err "bad_usage" "missing <name> — usage: k2 agent retire <name> [flags]"
        exit 2
    fi
    # Resolve (name | path) with the standard exit-4 + did-you-mean.
    local conf rc=0
    conf=$(_agent_conf_fetch "$name") || rc=$?
    [ "$rc" -ne 0 ] && exit "$rc"
    CONF="$conf" ARCHIVE_TO="$archive_to" FORCE="$force" DRY_RUN="$dry_run" \
    AS_JSON="$as_json" ABASE="$BASE_URL" ATOKEN="$TOKEN" python3 - <<'PYEOF'
import json, os, sys
import urllib.error, urllib.parse, urllib.request

conf = json.loads(os.environ["CONF"])
archive_to = os.environ.get("ARCHIVE_TO", "")
if archive_to:
    archive_to = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(archive_to))
force = os.environ.get("FORCE") == "true"
dry_run = os.environ.get("DRY_RUN") == "true"
as_json = os.environ.get("AS_JSON") == "true"
base = os.environ["ABASE"]
token = os.environ["ATOKEN"]
path = conf["path"]
label = conf.get("name") or os.path.basename(path)

url = base + "/cli/agent/retire?token=" + urllib.parse.quote(token, safe="")
body = json.dumps({"q": path, "force": force, "dryRun": dry_run,
                   "archiveTo": archive_to}).encode()
req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=body,
                             headers={"Content-Type": "application/json"}, method="POST")
try:
    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=120) as r:
        d = json.loads(r.read().decode("utf-8", "replace"))
except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
    try:
        d = json.loads(e.read().decode("utf-8", "replace"))
    except Exception:
        sys.stderr.write(json.dumps({"error": {"code": "daemon_error",
            "hint": "HTTP %s on /cli/agent/retire" % e.code}}) + "\n")
        sys.exit(1)
except Exception as e:
    sys.stderr.write(json.dumps({"error": {"code": "daemon_unreachable",
        "hint": "no response from the K2 daemon: %s" % e}}) + "\n")
    sys.exit(1)

err = d.get("error")
if d.get("refused"):
    # Safety guard tripped — the contract's exit 3, never a prompt.
    hint = (err or {}).get("hint") or "retire refused by a safety guard"
    if as_json:
        sys.stderr.write(json.dumps(d) + "\n")
    else:
        sys.stderr.write("REFUSED: %s\n" % hint)
        if d.get("dryRun"):
            sys.stderr.write("(dry-run: this is the verdict a real run would produce)\n")
    sys.exit(3)
if err:
    if isinstance(err, str):
        err = {"code": "daemon_error", "hint": err}
    sys.stderr.write(json.dumps({"error": err}) + "\n")
    sys.exit(4 if err.get("code") == "not_found" else 1)
if not d.get("ok"):
    sys.stderr.write(json.dumps({"error": {"code": "daemon_error",
        "hint": "unexpected response: %s" % json.dumps(d)[:300]}}) + "\n")
    sys.exit(1)

if as_json:
    print(json.dumps(d))
    sys.exit(0)

if d.get("dryRun"):
    print("DRY RUN — no changes made. Plan for retiring %s (%s):" % (label, path))
for a in d.get("actions", []):
    step, status = a.get("step", "?"), a.get("status", "?")
    detail = ""
    if step == "stop-session" and a.get("sessionId"):
        detail = " (session %s)" % str(a["sessionId"])[:8]
    elif step == "remove-connections" and a.get("removed") is not None:
        detail = " (%s edge(s))" % a["removed"]
    elif step == "remove-connections" and a.get("edges") is not None:
        detail = " (%s edge(s))" % a["edges"]
    elif step == "clean-dependents" and a.get("chatSessionNames") is not None:
        detail = " (%s chat-session row(s))" % a["chatSessionNames"]
    elif step == "archive-folder" and a.get("to"):
        detail = " → %s" % a["to"]
    if status == "skipped" and a.get("reason"):
        detail += "  (%s)" % a["reason"]
    marker = {"pending": "would apply", "done": "done", "skipped": "skipped",
              "failed": "FAILED"}.get(status, status)
    print("  %-14s %s%s" % ("[" + marker + "]", step, detail))
if not d.get("dryRun"):
    dest = d.get("archivedTo")
    if dest:
        print("%s retired — folder archived to %s (nothing was deleted)." % (label, dest))
    else:
        print("%s retired." % label)
PYEOF
}

cmd_help_skills() {
    cat <<'EOF'
k2 skills <subcommand> [options]

Manage documentation profiles (skills) for the workspace. Skills are
markdown files (SKILL.md) describing roles, personas, and instructions
your harness loads when spawning sub-agents.

  list                              Skill profiles in this workspace
  create <name> [--template <src>]  Create a new skill profile
                                    (optionally seeded from another skill)
  remove <name>                     Delete a skill profile (sent to Trash)
  profile <name>                    Read the skill's SKILL.md
  regenerate                        Refresh every skill's SKILL.md

SKILLS vs AGENT
  An agent IS a workspace (1:1). A skill is a documentation profile
  the agent (or your harness) can reference when applying a specific
  role to work.

  Spawning sessions pre-loaded with a skill is your harness's job
  (Claude Code's sub-agent spawning, Cursor's worktree management).
  K2SO no longer provides a `delegate` verb — see `k2 help-deprecated`.

  Skills live at `.k2/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (consolidated home as of
  Phase 2.5b). The legacy `.k2so/agents/` and `.k2so/agent-templates/`
  folders are migrated into here on first daemon boot per upgraded
  workspace. Originals go to the macOS Recycle Bin (recoverable).

TEMPLATING (post-Phase-2.5b)
  Any existing skill can seed a new one — there is no separate
  "template" namespace. `--template <name>` means "copy this skill as
  the starting point for the new skill." Edit the new file freely from
  there; the seed is unaffected.

EXAMPLES
  k2 skills list
  k2 skills create backend-eng --template rust-eng
  k2 skills profile backend-eng
  k2 skills regenerate
EOF
}

